\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Acceptance-rule sensitivity on the oracle-scored candidates (MPIR seed 1, Tier-1 seed-42 cells). Cells accepting: cells in which the rule accepts some candidate, out of the cells with at least one validated candidate. Mean delta is the mean change in strict test accuracy of the selected prompt versus P0, in points, over all cells with at least one validated candidate (a cell in which the rule accepts nothing counts as zero; for the larger gate, measured on the held-out half of the test split). Better/worse is the number of cells with a positive or negative delta.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
